{"id":"n5-127","title":"ほとんど〜 (hotondo〜)","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Used to express 'almost', 'nearly', or 'most'.","longExplanation":"The ほとんど〜 grammar point is used to express that something is 'almost', 'nearly', or 'most'. It can appear in both negative contexts (hardly/barely) or positive contexts (almost all). It is typically followed by a verb or used with a noun to describe the quantity or extent of something.","formation":"ほとんど + Verb / ほとんど + Noun","examples":[{"jp":"彼女はほとんど英語を話せません。","romaji":"Kanojo wa hotondo eigo o hanasemasen.","en":"She can hardly speak English.","words":[{"surface":"彼女","vocabId":"1483150","reading":"かのじょ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ほとんど","vocabId":"1522050","reading":"ほとんど"},{"surface":"英語","vocabId":"1174420","reading":"えいご"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"話せ","vocabId":"1562360","reading":"はなせる"},{"surface":"ませ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ん","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}]},{"jp":"ほとんどの人がパーティーに出席しました。","romaji":"Hotondo no hito ga paatii ni shusseki shimashita.","en":"Most people attended the party.","words":[{"surface":"ほとんど","vocabId":"1522050","reading":"ほとんど"},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"人","vocabId":"1580640","reading":"ひと"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"パーティー","vocabId":null},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"出席","vocabId":"1339460","reading":"しゅっせき"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}]},{"jp":"私たちはほとんど勉強しないでテストに合格しました。","romaji":"Watashitachi wa hotondo benkyou shinaide tesuto ni goukaku shimashita.","en":"We passed the test with hardly any studying.","words":[{"surface":"私","vocabId":"1311110","reading":"わたし"},{"surface":"たち","vocabId":"1416220","reading":"たち"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ほとんど","vocabId":"1522050","reading":"ほとんど"},{"surface":"勉強","vocabId":"1512670","reading":"べんきょう"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":